### *Part 2: Design Philosophy Summary*

*Why Pydantic not own validator?*
Don't reinvent wheel - Pydantic already uses Python type hints perfectly, battle-tested, fast (Rust core). FastAPI leverages it to get validation + serialization + docs from single source of truth.

*Why auto docs?*
In Flask/Django REST you write code THEN write Swagger separately - drifts. FastAPI generates OpenAPI from type hints at runtime - docs can never be outdated. Solves documentation hell.

*Why type hints everywhere?*
3 benefits from one hint:
1. Validation at runtime
2. Editor autocomplete
3. Auto docs
Python created type hints in 2015, FastAPI is first framework to fully exploit them.

*Why async-first?*
Flask synchronous = one request blocks thread. FastAPI on Starlette + async = can handle 1000s concurrent I/O (DB calls, API calls) on single thread. Built for modern microservices where you wait on network. Still supports sync `def` if you need.

*My mental model:* FastAPI philosophy = *explicit types = less code*. If you type it, you don't need to validate it, document it, or serialize it separately.

